INPUT: residues a[0..2p-2], prime p
  sort indices by residue, giving sorted values b[0..2p-2]
  for i in 0 .. (len - p):
      if b[i] == b[i+p-1]:
          return the p indices of this equal window  // sum = p*b[i] ≡ 0
  // no equal window: use gaps
  chosen <- {anchor index of b[0]};  running <- b[0] mod p
  for i in 1 .. p-1:
      lo <- b[i]; hi <- b[i+p-1]
      pick whichever of lo, hi keeps running prefix sum reachable mod p
      append its index to chosen; update running
  if running ≡ 0 (mod p): return chosen
  else: fall back to exhaustive search (guaranteed to succeed)
OUTPUT: p indices whose residues sum to 0 mod p

